+
+// validReferenceName rejects reference names that cannot safely be turned into
+// a path under the .git directory. A loose reference (and its reflog) is
+// stored verbatim at ".git/<name>", so a crafted name could otherwise climb out
+// of its reference sub-tree or land on unrelated repository metadata such as
+// .git/config, .git/hooks or .git/objects.
+//
